    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **45 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors** \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `checkDigit` as a read-time derived field \u2014 a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode` \u2014 following the same pattern as the other derived fields (`membershipLevel`, `locality`, `contactPreference`).\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient` `getCheckDigit()` getter that runs the Luhn algorithm over the digits of `customerCode` (skipping non-digit characters like the `-` separators), returning `null` when there's no `customerCode`.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared the read-only `checkDigit` field (integer, 0\u20139) on the owner schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct auto-maps it by name from the new getter.\n\nNo new function classes or YAML pipelines were needed \u2014 since `checkDigit` is purely derived from an already-stored field, it fits the existing read-time-derived convention rather than the create-pipeline assignment used for stored values like `customerCode` and `membershipNumber`.",
